<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Churchill returns three weeks after his stroke and two weeks after his first visit, on the day after his 21-day course of aspirin with clopidogrel ended. Physical and occupational therapy began last week. His left leg is stronger and he walks indoors without the stick; his left hand is still clumsy with buttons and writing, and his speech slurs only when he is tired. His home blood pressure has been 136 to 142 over 78 to 82 on amlodipine 10 mg, without lightheadedness. He has had no new weakness, numbness, speech change, or visual symptoms, and no bleeding or bruising. He has cut down to about five cigars a day but is drinking as before. His mood is a little better, though he still becomes tearful when moved. He saw neurology this morning, and a 30-day heart monitor was fitted. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Interval change</td><td>Leg stronger; walking indoors without a stick; hand still clumsy</td></tr><tr><td>Home blood pressure</td><td>136 to 142 over 78 to 82 on amlodipine 10 mg</td></tr><tr><td>Antiplatelet therapy</td><td>Aspirin stopped yesterday after 21 days; clopidogrel continues; no bleeding</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco and alcohol</td><td>About five cigars a day; drinking unchanged</td></tr><tr><td>Mood</td><td>Slightly better; still tearful when moved</td></tr><tr><td>Rehabilitation</td><td>Physical and occupational therapy twice weekly since last week</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

