<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Right-hemisphere lacunar stroke three weeks ago, improving (I69.354)</content>. Recovering steadily. Neurology confirms a small-vessel lacunar infarct and agrees with clopidogrel alone after the 21-day course. A 30-day ambulatory ECG monitor was fitted today. [S]<list><item>Continue clopidogrel 75 mg daily and atorvastatin 80 mg daily.</item><item>Continue physical and occupational therapy.</item><item>Lipid panel and monitor result at the eight-week review.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Essential hypertension (I10)</content>. Blood pressure 138/80 mmHg on amlodipine 10 mg, above the 130/80 target, without orthostatic fall. [S]<list><item>Add lisinopril 5 mg daily.</item><item>Basic metabolic panel in one to two weeks.</item><item>Home blood pressure seated and standing.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Nicotine dependence, cigars (F17.290)</content>. Down from six to eight to about five cigars a day. [S]<list><item>Encouraged to keep cutting down; nicotine replacement offered and declined.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Unhealthy alcohol use</content>. AUDIT-C 8 two weeks ago; no change in drinking. [S]<list><item>Brief intervention: no more than two drinks a day; alcohol raises blood pressure and the risk of another stroke and of falls.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Blood pressure seated and standing, weight and BMI</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Seated 138/80 mmHg, standing 134/78 mmHg; weight 79.6 kg; above the 130/80 target</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Short-course dual antiplatelet therapy</td><td>21 to 90 days after a minor noncardioembolic stroke, then a single antiplatelet</td><td>Completed today</td><td>21 days of aspirin with clopidogrel completed yesterday; clopidogrel continues alone; no bleeding</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Antithrombotic and statin adherence</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Taking clopidogrel and atorvastatin every day</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Prolonged cardiac rhythm monitoring</td><td>At least 30 days within 6 months of the stroke</td><td>Ordered</td><td>30-day ambulatory ECG monitor fitted today at the neurology consultation</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Baseline 12-lead ECG</td><td>Once after the event</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Sinus rhythm with left ventricular hypertrophy at the first visit</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Lipid panel</td><td>4 to 12 weeks after starting or changing a statin, then every 3 to 12 months</td><td>Due</td><td>Atorvastatin started three weeks ago; due at the eight-week review</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Basic metabolic panel</td><td>1 to 2 weeks after starting an ACE inhibitor, then every 6 months</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Lisinopril started today; panel ordered for one to two weeks from now</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>NIH Stroke Scale</td><td>At presentation and with any change</td><td>Completed today</td><td>1 (mild left arm drift), down from 2</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Fall-risk assessment</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No falls; walking indoors without a stick</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Physical and occupational therapy</td><td>At discharge and through recovery</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Twice weekly since last week</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Neurology consultation</td><td>After the event</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Seen today</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Depression screen (PHQ-9)</td><td>First post-stroke visit, then periodically while symptoms persist; at least yearly</td><td>Up to date</td><td>8 at the first visit two weeks ago, item 9 scored 0; repeat at the eight-week review</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Cognitive screen (MoCA)</td><td>After the event, again within the first year</td><td>Up to date</td><td>26 at the first visit; repeat within the year</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Tobacco use</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>About five cigars a day; advice to stop; nicotine replacement declined</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Alcohol use</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Drinking unchanged; brief intervention given</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Physical activity</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Walking in the house and garden twice a day as therapy advises</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Obstructive sleep apnea evaluation</td><td>Consider for all after stroke</td><td>Due</td><td>Screening questions planned at the eight-week review</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Lower blood pressure below 130/80 mmHg without orthostatic symptoms by the eight-week review. In progress; target 2026-08-19 [S]</item><item>Lower LDL cholesterol below 70 mg/dL by the eight-week review. In progress; target 2026-08-19 [S]</item><item>Return to full work and public speaking by about three months after the stroke. In progress; target 2026-10-07 [S]</item><item>Keep to no more than two drinks on any day. In progress; target 2026-10-07 [S]</item><item>Cut down to three cigars a day as a step toward stopping. In progress; target 2026-10-07 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: 2021 Guideline for the Prevention of Stroke in Patients With Stroke and Transient Ischemic Attack (2021); Primary Care of Adult Patients After Stroke: A Scientific Statement From the American Heart Association/American Stroke Association (2021); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, stroke/TIA, hypertension, and depression monographs (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Basic metabolic panel in one to two weeks. Stroke review in five weeks with a lipid panel and the monitor result. Call 911 for any new stroke symptom. Next scheduled visit 2026-08-19: eight-week stroke and blood pressure review with lipid panel and rhythm-monitor results. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
